nd of  like a  thing of like the asian american version  of boys in the hood so it's like an  asian gangster movie  but not with triads it's more about  street gangs  and it's about  these two friends  who  one kid comes from a rich family and the  other kid is um  from a poor family but he's in the gang  and the rich kid wants to join the gang  and be a part of that lifestyle whereas  the the um the gangster kid wants to get  out of that lifestyle and he wants to  become a dj and pursue creative path  but you know their two paths kind of  you know break apart their friendship  and there's all this drama that happens  along with that  and that was shot where  oh we filmed that in san diego  okay but it was supposed to take place  in san diego um i didn't really wanted  to have a specific place that it was um  you know taking place in  but  it definitely has like a west coast kind  of feel  um so a lot of people actually recognize  the locations um and they're like oh  that's san diego this is where i grew up  but yeah yeah yeah it's always an  interesting mix of and i've seen that  before especially if you know in the bay  area there's a lot of great wealth but  you'll see the  few people that actually maybe are  almost ashamed of it and and sort of  want that street life and then of course  you know people that don't come from  that always envy  the opposite so yeah it's an interesting  uh interesting mix yeah  what does success mean to you now  success now  is really just about you know living a  a peaceful life uh um  a happy life  and not necessarily chasing after  wealth or um  you know material things and that has a  lot to do with um like a few years ago  i kind of got  um you know introduced to buddhism  and some of the ideas and philosophies  behind that um you know i went to  meditation retreat  and kind of like woke me up a little bit  in terms of like what's actually  important and what and what am i really  doing you know in this world  so now it's real